WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.771 --> 00:00:12.341
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> How do people read today? Where do they read, and what kinds of things?

2
00:00:13.378 --> 00:00:30.928
People read many different things in their free time: books, newspapers, magazines, maybe subtitles.

3
00:00:31.987 --> 00:00:44.436
They read things when they’re studying, or at work: documents, websites, textbooks or manuals.

4
00:00:44.781 --> 00:01:00.299
People read in different places and at different times: on the bus or train, in bed, or on holiday.

5
00:01:01.639 --> 00:01:12.921
Sometimes people read in another language: graded readers, or song lyrics.

6
00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:18.216
People read in different ways today.

7
00:01:18.886 --> 00:01:24.138
They read on paper or on screen.

8
00:01:25.997 --> 00:01:30.557
People read all kinds of things in all kinds of places!

9
00:01:30.989 --> 00:01:32.178
What about you?